  /// Identity used to be inferred by matching the session email's local part
  /// against studentNo, which let anyone with a chosen email read another
  /// child's records.
  userId          String?
  studentNo       String
  admissionNo     String?
  firstName       String
  lastName        String
  dateOfBirth     DateTime?
  gender          String?
  status          SchoolStudentStatus @default(APPLICANT)
  currentClassId  String?
  currentStreamId String?
  isBoarding      Boolean             @default(false)
  admissionDate   DateTime?
  /// S-4.3 — the record page's identity strip.
  ///
  /// A photograph when there is one; otherwise the initials `PersonAvatar`
  /// derives from the name. `accent` pins the name-derived colour so the same
  /// person is the same colour on the register, the mark sheet and the record
  /// page; null means it keeps taking its colour from the name.
  ///
  /// Deliberately no `emoji` column, unlike the CRM record types: a child or a
  /// parent is a person, and offering to stand one in as 🙂 is not a feature.
  avatarUrl       String?
  accent          String?
  /// S-4.4 — the school's own fields on this record, keyed by
  /// `CrmFieldDefinition.key`.
  ///
  /// A JSON column rather than an entity-attribute-value table, matching what
  /// the CRM records already do: the definitions carry the types and the
